Yani for a new G monster: The gastrognome.

The gastrognome is no tougher than your regular gnome, but he is armed
with a stack of cream pies which, as we all know, can be a real pain
to early pre-telepathy characters, especially in the mines. However
they do tend to waste ther time trailing around the level looking for
food to pick up, so they aren't all that dangerous.
Killing a gastrognome is likely to yield a surprising quantity and
variety of interesting food items - cream pies, meatballs, fruit &
veg, fortune cookies, !oBooze and so on. They might also carry the odd
?ofood detection. No cram rations or food rations (too bland), no
corpses (As we all know, they taste "terrible") and no tinned food
(gastrognomes only like fresh food.) Due to this exquisite diet,
gastrognome corpses are invariably delicious, but the intrinsic
appetite of the unfortunate creature has been known to be magically
transferred to the devourer.

Players polymorphed into gastrognomes would get all kinds of
interesting messages when eating:
"The yellow potion tastes of summer fields, with a lingering
aftertaste of berries."
"This red dragon corpse tastes smoky, with a hint of oak and burnt
peasant."

I would also suggest the addition of a new weapon, specially for the
gastrognome: The sharpened banana. This deadly fruit is at least as
effective as a dagger when thrown (as demonstrated by Dr Bunsen
Honeydew on a muppet show DVD I saw recently) but somewhat less
effective at hand-to-hand range (as demonstrated in a certain python
sketch).
Anyone can create a sharpened banana of course, as long as they have
(a) a banana and (b) something to sharpen it with. A sword or knife
would do. As well as being deadly weapons, SBs have the added bonus of
being convenient snacks (albeit slightly less filling than blunt
bananas - some of the fruit is lost in the sharpening process.)

Finally, a question: Why does slashem have cream pies that can be used
as projectile weapons, and firearms, but no bugsy malone-style splurge
guns?

